&lt;div&gt;The Group Manager, Astranis Products will lead procurement activities for Astranis designed hardware manufactured through contract manufacturers and external production partners. This individual will oversee supplier execution for high-volume, production-critical components including machined parts, electronics, and assemblies. The Group Manager will partner closely with Production, Supplier Quality, Manufacturing Engineering, and Supply Chain teams to ensure suppliers consistently deliver high-quality materials on schedule. The ideal candidate is experienced in fast-paced manufacturing environments and excels at driving supplier performance, resolving production challenges, and building strong operational partnerships.&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div&gt;The ideal candidate will be an accomplished leader who has expertise in the Purchasing discipline as well as other business functions in a manufacturing environment. This person should possess a minimum of 5 years of purchasing/supply chain experience with at least 2 years at the management level. This individual must demonstrate well-rounded business acumen, the ability to develop people and not be afraid to roll up their sleeves to get the job done.&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Role&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop, document, and execute sourcing strategies that utilize negotiation and purchasing techniques ensuring the very best quality, cost, delivery, and service.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manage supplier relations and supply agreement compliance while maintaining the highest code of ethics and conduct.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Oversees cradle-to-grave process from intent to purchase, new supplier on-boarding, performance, and supplier exit. Tracks supplier performance using dashboards for quality, delivery, service and cost.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deliver aggressive cost reduction objectives, partnering closely with production, engineering, quality, and program management&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Continuously analyze market and delivery conditions to ensure present and future material availability.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work with Production, Supplier Quality and Engineering to develop product specifications and source new components.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Identify and evaluate new/increased sources of supply that support plant expansions, new products, and sustainability objectives.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;div&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Requirements &lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bachelor’s degree in Business, Supply Chain, Operations Management, Engineering or Chemistry and/or equivalent experience or evidence of exceptional ability.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Master’s degree in Business, Supply Chain, Operations Management, or Engineering preferred.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Expertise in world class procurement operations and how to get there. Capable of driving change while maintaining positive internal relations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong knowledge of generally accepted purchasing and accounting practices, contract negotiation, related laws and regulations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Supplier scorecard techniques that drive supplier management.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent leadership, negotiation, analytical, and problem solving skills. Passion for results, strategy, and execution. Creative, calculated risk taker.&lt;/li&gt;
