&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;Astranis builds advanced satellites for high orbits, expanding humanity’s reach into the solar system. Today, Astranis satellites provide dedicated, secure networks to highly-sophisticated customers across the globe— large enterprises, sovereign governments, and the US military. With five satellites on orbit and many more set to launch soon, the company is servicing a backlog of more than $1 billion of commercial contracts.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Astranis is the preferred satellite communications partner for buyers with stringent requirements for uptime, data security, network visibility, and customization. Astranis has raised over $750 million from some of the world’s best investors, from Andreessen Horowitz to Blackrock and Fidelity, and employs a team of 450 engineers and entrepreneurs. Astranis designs, builds, and operates its satellites out of its 153,000 sq. ft. headquarters in Northern California, USA.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Team Lead - RF Integration&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As the Production RF Integration Team Lead, you will build, mentor, and guide a high-performing team of engineers dedicated to the assembly, integration, and testing (AI&amp;amp;T) of Astranis spacecraft payloads and RF sub-assemblies. This role bridges the gap between RF design and flight-ready production. You will oversee the development of RF test cells, design-for-test (DFT) strategies, and cross-functional processes that ensure our communication satellites meet rigorous performance metrics before launch.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This role requires a unique blend of deep technical RF knowledge &amp;amp; intuition, agile program management, and people-first leadership.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Role&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hire, develop, and lead a world-class team of RF test engineers. Cultivate a culture of technical excellence, safety, and continuous learning.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Oversee the design and implementation of hardware test racks, leveraging both COTS equipment and custom PCBAs to measure complex RF signals, apply flight-like loads, and power units under test.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Drive the development of Python-based automation software to interface with flight hardware, RF test equipment (VNAs, spectrum analyzers), and enterprise data systems for seamless data capture.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Stand up and scale cross-functional business processes for RF test requirements capture, test development, and rigorous test validation.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner closely with RF Design, Mechanical Integration, and Environmental Test teams to channel test insights back into design improvements&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manage budgets, schedules, work plans, and performance requirements to ensure production milestones are met without sacrificing quality&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Requirements&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;B.S. in Electrical Engineering, Aerospace Engineering, or a related technical discipline.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;5+ years of professional experience in a fast-paced hardware product development or production environment&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven track record of building, managing, and mentoring engineering teams, with a knack for delegation and team building&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong Design-for-Test (DFT) and test automation mindset, specifically tailored to complex hardware&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Exceptional ability to synthesize and summarize dense, highly technical RF and systems topics for both executive leadership and cross-functional teams&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated ability to build engineering and operational processes from scratch&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;US Citizenship or Permanent Residency (Green Card) is required&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to work 5 days a week in office&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Bonus&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Direct experience with RF test and measurement equipment (Vector Network Analyzers, Spectrum Analyzers, Noise Figure Meters, Signal Generators).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proficiency in Python or C++ for test automation and data analysis.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with the space environment, aerospace hardware integration, and test flows (TVAC, Vibration, EMI/EMC).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience managing a mixed team of both engineers and technicians in a production environment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Knowledge of Digital Signal Processing (DSP) and digital communication systems&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-pay-transparency&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-input&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;description&quot;&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What we offer:&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
